# rules: go-secret-compared-in-variable-time
# languages: go
# fixture: go/CWE-208.go
# from: CWE-208 (Observable Timing Discrepancy), CWE-1254, CWE-697
#
# Go's string and []byte equality stops at the first byte that differs, so the
# comparison takes longer the longer the common prefix is. Against somebody
# who can time it and retry, that turns guessing a 32-byte MAC from 2^256 work
# into 256 * 32, one byte at a time.
#
# A comparison does not say what it is comparing, so the rule reads the names,
# and the word list is the whole rule. `token` on its own is not in it: in Go
# a token is overwhelmingly a lexer's token, and including it reported
# `len(tokens) == 0` and `StopReason == "max_tokens"` across every parser in
# reach. The qualified spellings - auth_token, session_token, csrf_token and
# the rest - say what the bare word does not.
#
# Comparisons against a literal, against nil, against a bool and of a length
# are subtracted. None of them leaks a prefix: asking whether a secret was
# supplied at all is not comparing it to another secret, a length is one
# number however long the secret is, and a secret compared against something
# written in the source is the hardcoded-credential rule's business rather
# than this one's. A whole-literal test rather than a leading-quote one, so
# that `hdr == "Bearer "+accessToken` - which is this bug - still counts.
#
# Anything naming an algorithm or a scheme is subtracted too, and that guard
# earns its place: `signature` is in the word list, s2a-go compares
# `signatureAlgorithm` against a dozen enum constants in one switch, and
# comparing which algorithm was chosen leaks nothing about any key.

["$A == $B", "$A != $B"] as $compares
| ["$A == \"\"", "$A != \"\"", "\"\" == $A", "\"\" != $A",
   "$A == nil", "$A != nil", "nil == $A", "nil != $A",
   "len($_) == $_", "len($_) != $_", "$_ == len($_)", "$_ != len($_)",
   "$A == true", "$A != true", "$A == false", "$A != false",
   "subtle.ConstantTimeCompare($$$_) == $_",
   "subtle.ConstantTimeCompare($$$_) != $_",
   "hmac.Equal($$$_) == $_", "hmac.Equal($$$_) != $_"] as $notASecret
| scan_ast("*.go"; $compares + $notASecret) as $all
| ( $all | of($compares)
    | where_text("(?i:secret|password|passwd|passphrase|signature|hmac"
                 + "|apikey|api_key|authkey|auth_key|credential"
                 + "|auth_?token|access_?token|session_?token|bearer_?token"
                 + "|refresh_?token|csrf_?token|api_?token)|MAC")
    | where_text_not("(?i)algorithm|scheme")
    | where_capture_not("A"; "^\"[^\"]*\"$")
    | where_capture_not("B"; "^\"[^\"]*\"$")
    | not_at($all | of($notASecret)) )
| finding("go-secret-compared-in-variable-time";
    "== stops at the first byte that differs, so this comparison takes longer "
    + "the more of the secret is right; subtle.ConstantTimeCompare or "
    + "hmac.Equal instead")
| report
